<h2>2. What are cookies?</h2>
<p>Cookies are small text files that websites store on the User&#x27;s device (computer, smartphone, tablet) when visited. They make it possible to remember information about the visit, recognise the User on subsequent visits and offer specific functionalities.</p>
<p>In a broad sense, the term &quot;cookies&quot; also covers similar technologies such as the browser&#x27;s local storage (localStorage) or tracking pixels.</p>
<h2>3. Types of cookies used</h2>
<p>By their ownership, cookies may be first-party (managed directly by Amber Muscle) or third-party (managed by an external provider).</p>
<p>By their duration, they may be session cookies (deleted when the browser is closed) or persistent (remaining for a determined period).</p>
<p>By their purpose, they may be:</p>
<p>Technical: necessary for the proper functioning of the Website. Do not require consent.</p>
<p>Preferences or personalisation: allow remembering User settings (language, visual theme, etc.). Do not require consent.</p>
<p>Analytical or measurement: allow analysing User behaviour in aggregate form. Require prior consent.</p>
<p>Advertising: NOT used on this Website.</p>
